cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite it using the metadata below,
  together with the accompanying article.
type: software
title: >-
  asc-semantic-map: code for "How do children with autism perceive the
  external world? Cortex-wide mapping of visual semantic representation"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived data for Lee et al. The pipelines map
  whole-brain semantic representations from movie-watching fMRI in
  children with and without autism (Healthy Brain Network) using a
  gaze-informed encoding model, and reproduce the semantic-axis,
  representational-dimensionality, symptom-prediction, normative-modelling,
  structural-equation-modelling and subtyping analyses from the encoding
  weights onwards.
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jelee2498/asc-semantic-map"
keywords:
  - autism
  - fMRI
  - naturalistic viewing
  - semantic representation
  - encoding model
  - eye tracking
  - normative modelling
